  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=2x+4$ and $y=4-x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2x+4 & \\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}y-2 \\\\ y=4-x & \\,\u27f9\\,x=4-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/da7778322523d0d18a5d5e24af075709958d329fc0053c836fd6637aa912752d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}y-2\\le x\\le 4-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2-2}^{4-y}x{e}^{y}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
